  "finalText": "T-1070 is re-graded and escalated, but I did not close it. T-1071 is linked to it and still open, and policy blocks closing while a linked ticket is open.\n\n- **Severity:** raised from sev3 to sev1. The matrix gives payroll at company-wide scope as sev1, regardless of how urgently Grace asked.\n- **Deadline:** unchanged at 2026-03-17T19:40Z. That deadline was already committed to the requester, and recomputing it as now plus 60 minutes would have moved it earlier.\n- **Escalation:** sent to incident-command. E-402 Ola Berg is the engineer on call there when the deadline falls. The ticket status is now `escalated`.\n- **Assignee:** the escalation made E-402 the assignee. My plan was to keep E-201 as assignee. E-201 Ines Kovac (business-apps, the rotation that owns payroll) is on call until 20:00Z, and the handover comment records her role.\n- **Handover comment:** it names T-1071 as the blocker and records the sev1 re-grade, the escalation and the unchanged deadline. It gives the next steps: fix T-1071, rerun the March batch, confirm payments post, then close. It also notes that payday is Friday.\n- **T-1071:** I left it untouched, since it is outside this request. The comment flags that it is assigned to E-101 Dana Whitfield and due at 10:30Z. The next shift should check that she is in the business-apps rotation.\n\nGrace needs to be told that it can't be closed today, because T-1071 has to be fixed first and the batch rerun.",
